# Line-ending normalization (ADR "Repo-wide line-ending normalization"). Git stores every text file with LF and
# checks it out with LF on every platform, so the `.editorconfig` `end_of_line = lf` + the CI `dotnet format`
# whitespace gate (ADR 0439) can never be fought by a CRLF checkout. `text=auto` auto-detects binary files and
# leaves them byte-for-byte untouched; the explicit `binary` markers below are belt-and-suspenders for the asset
# types we ship so a line-ending conversion can never corrupt them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize.
*.png   binary
*.icns  binary
*.ico   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.snk   binary
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary
